# Cursor AI Rules - ProCPX Procurement System

## 🛡️ Gitignore Auto-Update Policy
- Proactively inspect and auto-update `.gitignore` whenever introducing new files, dependencies, build outputs, certificates, secret files, or temporary caches.
- Never commit `.env` or sensitive secret credentials.

## 📝 Structured Detailed Logging Standards
- Integrate structured detailed logging using `import { logger } from '@/lib/logger'` across all API routes, state actions, services, and components.
- Do not use raw `console.*` calls in application code.
- Always include `module`, `message`, structured metadata (`data`), and `correlationId`.
- Server logs are persisted to `logs/app.log` and `logs/error.log` with automatic 5MB rotation and 7-day purging.
- Logs can be searched or purged via `/api/logs`.

## 📦 Separate Constants Architecture & Standards
- Keep all constants, lookup tables, and mock datasets in separate files under `src/constants/` (`tenants.ts`, `procurement.ts`, `vendors.ts`, `boq.ts`, `masters.ts`, `navigation.ts`, `ai.ts`, `logging.ts`, `database.ts`, `graphql.ts`, `crypto.ts`, `diagnostics.ts`, `validation.ts`).
- Never define inline mock datasets, configuration dictionaries, or constant lists in components, hooks, or context files.
- Always import constants via the central `@/constants` alias.

## 🏷️ Separate Data Types & Interfaces Architecture & Standards
- Declare all TypeScript types, interfaces, enums, and type aliases in separate files under `src/types/` (`procurement.ts`, `context.ts`, `components.ts`, `ai.ts`, `logger.ts`, `database.ts`, `graphql.ts`, `crypto.ts`, `diagnostics.ts`, `validation.ts`).
- Never define inline `interface` or `type` declarations inside components or runtime files.
- Always import types via the central `@/types` alias.

## ⚡ Database Optimization & Compute Minimization Standards
- Audit database queries with `dbAuditor` (`src/lib/db-auditor.ts`) and Prisma query middleware.
- Flag queries $\ge 100\text{ms}$ as slow queries and log via `logger.warn`.
- Use read-through caching (`dbCache` in `src/lib/db-cache.ts`) with tag invalidation to reduce database compute hours.
- Enforce selective projections (avoid `SELECT *`) and prevent N+1 query loops.

## 🌐 GraphQL Integration & Streamlined Data Fetching
- Provide a unified GraphQL API at `/api/graphql` with schema in `src/graphql/schema.ts` and resolvers in `src/graphql/resolvers.ts`.
- Streamline client queries by fetching exact selection sets without over/under-fetching.
- Apply complexity and size bounds (`GRAPHQL_COMPLEXITY_LIMITS`).
- Connect resolvers to `dbCache` and invalidate tags on mutations.

## 🔐 AES Encryption & Data Protection Standards
- Use **AES-256-GCM** authenticated encryption (`DEFAULT_AES_ALGORITHM`) as the default cryptographic standard.
- Derive keys via **PBKDF2** with HMAC-SHA256, 100,000 iterations, and unique 16-byte random salts.
- Require fresh nonces/IVs (12 bytes for GCM) and strictly verify 128-bit authentication tags on decryption.
- Support field-level encryption (`encryptFields()`) and deterministic blind indexing (`generateBlindIndex()`) for searchable encrypted fields.
- Never log plaintext secrets or keys in application logs; audit operations via `logger.debug`.

## 🐛 Auto-Resolve Bugs & Errors in Logs Standards
- Proactively monitor and analyze logs (`logs/error.log`, `logs/app.log`) to catch runtime defects.
- Use `src/lib/log-analyzer.ts` or `npm run logs:analyze` to parse stack frames, error codes, and correlation IDs.
- Execute verified bug fixes and auto-resolutions (`npm run logs:auto-resolve`) to prevent recurring failures.
- Validate all bug fixes through the mandatory quality check pipeline (`npm run check:all`) to guarantee zero regressions.

## 🛡️ Input Schema Validation Standards
- Enforce strict input schema validation across the application whenever any code touches user or system inputs.
- Validate all frontend forms, API route bodies, query parameters, controller arguments, and HTTP headers before processing.
- All validation schemas must be defined in dedicated constants modules under `src/constants/validation.ts` (0 inline schemas).
- All validation types must be declared in `src/types/validation.ts` (0 inline types).
- Use `src/lib/validator.ts`: `validateSchema()`, `validateQueryParams()`, `validateHeaders()`.
- Return structured 400 errors for API validation failures and prevent invalid state transitions.

## 🌐 Internationalization (i18n) & UI Strings Architecture Standards (See: `.agents/rules/i18n-standards.md`)
- Strictly enforce i18n readiness across the application: zero hardcoded user-facing strings, labels, or literals embedded directly in JSX/TSX or application code.
- All user-facing text, titles, descriptions, button labels, input placeholders, table headers, empty state notices, ARIA labels, and dialog copy must be declared in dedicated constants modules under `src/constants/strings.ts` and referenced via the centralized `UI_STRINGS` dictionary.
- Use template placeholders (e.g. `'{round}'`, `'{name}'`, `'{count}'`, `'{tenantName}'`) with the centralized `formatString(template, values)` helper for dynamic runtime substitution (never use inline concatenation or ad-hoc template literals).
- All UI string types and dictionary interfaces must be declared in `src/types/strings.ts` and exported via `@/types`.
- Modernize all unit and integration tests to assert against `UI_STRINGS` constants (and `formatString` templates) instead of hardcoded strings to prevent brittle matches during UI copy updates.
- Maintain strict $\ge 90\%$ code coverage across all metrics for i18n modules, helpers, and components.

## ⚡ Quality Check Execution After Every Change
- **Fast iterations on changed files**:
  `npm run check:fast`
  (Checks only modified files: tsc --noEmit, jest --onlyChanged, fast lint, prisma validate).
- **Before completing any task (Full Check)**:
  `npm run check:all`
  (Runs full quality check pipeline).
- **Workspace-wide check**:
  `npm run check:workspace`
  (Global check across all workspace projects).

## 🥇 Strict Check Order: Build & Coverage First
1. Build Verification: `npm run build`
2. Unit Test Coverage: `npm run test:coverage` (Strict 90% benchmark per file across lines, statements, branches, and functions)
3. Typecheck: `npm run typecheck`
4. Lint: `npm run lint`
5. Database Schema & Migrations: `npm run db:validate` / `npm run db:migrate`

## 🎯 90% Unit Test Code Coverage Benchmark
- 90% Unit Test Code Coverage is strictly enforced per file across lines, statements, branches, and functions.
- Do not skip any file in `src/`.
- Tests must use `--detectOpenHandles` and respect 30s timeout.

## 🔄 CI/CD Pull Request Pipeline & PR Comments
- Every PR triggers `.github/workflows/pull-request.yml` with a hard timeout of 20 minutes (`timeout-minutes: 20`).
- Validates: Production Build $\rightarrow$ Unit Test Coverage ($\ge 90\%$ per file across all 4 parameters) $\rightarrow$ Typecheck $\rightarrow$ Lint $\rightarrow$ Database validation.
- Automatically publishes/updates an idempotent PR comment with test pass/fail metrics and overall & per-file coverage breakdown (`npm run ci:summary`).

